* SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
* Necessary-condition screen for a selectable HCLK-derived WRITE window.
*
* This is intentionally a self-contained source-level probe.  It does not
* claim the complete pulse generator or its parent interconnect.  It proves
* only whether a static one-bit code can select between two *full-swing*
* HCLK-derived end states before narrow-pulse formation and still drive the
* existing 650-fF WRITE boundary at every declared PVT condition.

.include /foss/pdks/gf180mcuD/libs.tech/ngspice/design.ngspice
.lib /foss/pdks/gf180mcuD/libs.tech/ngspice/sm141064.ngspice @MOS_CORNER@
.temp @TEMP_C@

.subckt cp_inv A Y VDD VSS params: WP=4u WN=2u MP=1 MN=1
XP Y A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w={WP} l=0.28u m={MP}
XN Y A VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w={WN} l=0.28u m={MN}
.ends cp_inv

.subckt cp_delay A Y VDD VSS params: WP=4u WN=2u MP=2 MN=2
XI0 A D0 VDD VSS cp_inv WP={WP} WN={WN} MP={MP} MN={MN}
XI1 D0 Y VDD VSS cp_inv WP={WP} WN={WN} MP={MP} MN={MN}
.ends cp_delay

* A complementary transmission gate is permitted only here, while its
* signal is a long full-swing clock state.  Each selected state is restored
* by two CMOS stages before it is compared to the start state.
.subckt cp_tg A Y EN ENB VDD VSS params: W=8u M=2
XN Y EN A VSS nfet_03v3 w={W} l=0.28u m={M}
XP Y ENB A VDD pfet_03v3 w={W} l=0.28u m={M}
.ends cp_tg

.subckt cp_fall_window A B Y VDD VSS
XI B BN VDD VSS cp_inv WP=8u WN=8u MP=2 MN=2
XP0 YB A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=8u l=0.28u m=3
XP1 YB BN VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w=8u l=0.28u m=3
XN0 YB A NS VSS nfet_03v3 w=8u l=0.28u m=3
XN1 NS BN VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w=8u l=0.28u m=3
XIY YB Y VDD VSS cp_inv WP=8u WN=8u MP=4 MN=3
.ends cp_fall_window

.subckt cp_final_inv A Y VDD VSS params: WP=8u WN=8u MP=28 MN=22
XP Y A VDD VDD pfet_03v3 w={WP} l=0.28u m={MP}
XN Y A VSS VSS nfet_03v3 w={WN} l=0.28u m={MN}
.ends cp_final_inv

* SEL=0 selects the base end state.  SEL=1 selects the same regenerated
* state followed by one additional, physically realizable delay pair.  The
* state selection happens before the detector, so disabled diffusion never
* touches the WPN or WRITE narrow-event nets.
.subckt hclk_select_window HCLK SEL VDD VSS WRITE WPN
XI_SEL SEL SELB VDD VSS cp_inv WP=4u WN=2u MP=2 MN=2

* Matched full-swing source/selection paths: START is the reference edge;
* END0 and END1 differ solely by the calibrated extra delay state.  START
* includes a matched restoring pair, so the selection-restorer latency is not
* accidentally charged to the window budget.
XST0 HCLK S0A VDD VSS cp_delay WP=4u WN=2u MP=2 MN=2
XST1 HCLK S1A VDD VSS cp_delay WP=4u WN=2u MP=2 MN=2
XSTR0 S0A STR0 VDD VSS cp_inv WP=@START0_WP@ WN=@START0_WN@ MP=@START0_MP@ MN=@START0_MN@
XSTR1 STR0 START VDD VSS cp_inv WP=@START1_WP@ WN=@START1_WN@ MP=@START1_MP@ MN=@START1_MN@
XEND0 S0A E0 VDD VSS cp_delay WP=4u WN=2u MP=2 MN=2
XEND1A S1A E1A VDD VSS cp_delay WP=4u WN=2u MP=2 MN=2
XEND1B E1A E1 VDD VSS cp_delay WP=@EXTRA_W@ WN=@EXTRA_N@ MP=@EXTRA_MP@ MN=@EXTRA_MN@

* The unselected end's pass-device diffusion is isolated by the common
* restoring pair.  START is deliberately unselected: it gives both codes a
* fixed reference and makes the code's timing effect explicit and measurable.
XTG0 E0 EMUX SELB SEL VDD VSS cp_tg
XTG1 E1 EMUX SEL SELB VDD VSS cp_tg
XER0 EMUX ER0 VDD VSS cp_inv WP=8u WN=4u MP=2 MN=2
XER1 ER0 END VDD VSS cp_inv WP=8u WN=6u MP=3 MN=2

* Compare the matched, restored START state to the selected restored END
* state.  Do not bypass START with raw S0A: that would silently add the
* selection restorer latency to the interval being calibrated.
XDET START END WIN VDD VSS cp_fall_window
XWPN WIN WPN VDD VSS cp_inv WP=4u WN=4u MP=2 MN=2
XWB0 WPN WB1 VDD VSS cp_inv WP=4u WN=4u MP=2 MN=2
XWB1 WB1 WB2 VDD VSS cp_inv WP=4u WN=4u MP=4 MN=4
XWB2 WB2 WB3 VDD VSS cp_inv WP=8u WN=8u MP=4 MN=4
XWB3 WB3 WB4 VDD VSS cp_inv WP=8u WN=8u MP=8 MN=8
XWB4 WB4 WRITE VDD VSS cp_final_inv
.ends hclk_select_window

VDD VDD 0 PWL(0 0 500p @VDD_V@)
VSEL SEL 0 PWL(0 0 500p @SEL_V@)
* This is the full-swing parent HCLK contract used by the pulse macro.  The
* normal high state is 380 ps at the 800-ps unit interval; no behavioral
* delay source is used to form the selected narrow interval.
VHCLK HCLK 0 PULSE(0 @VDD_V@ 1n 20p 20p 380p 800p)
XDUT HCLK SEL VDD 0 WRITE WPN hclk_select_window
CWRITE WRITE 0 650f

.control
* The third post-ramp clock is sufficient for this entirely combinational
* probe; keeping the run short lets every PVT/code candidate be evaluated in
* one bounded campaign rather than silently sampling a subset.
tran 1p 3.6n uic
let isupply = -i(VDD)
meas tran hclk_fall when v(HCLK)=@VMID@ fall=1 td=2.8n
meas tran write_rise when v(WRITE)=@VMID@ rise=1 td=2.8n
meas tran write_fall when v(WRITE)=@VMID@ fall=1 td=2.8n
meas tran win_rise when v(XDUT.WIN)=@VMID@ rise=1 td=2.8n
meas tran win_fall when v(XDUT.WIN)=@VMID@ fall=1 td=2.8n
meas tran wpn_fall when v(WPN)=@VMID@ fall=1 td=2.8n
meas tran wpn_rise when v(WPN)=@VMID@ rise=1 td=2.8n
meas tran write_high max v(WRITE) from=2.8n to=3.6n
meas tran write_low min v(WRITE) from=2.8n to=3.6n
meas tran wpn_high max v(WPN) from=2.8n to=3.6n
meas tran wpn_low min v(WPN) from=2.8n to=3.6n
meas tran supply_current avg isupply from=2.8n to=3.6n
.endc
.end
